8.4 The Director of the Heritage Grants Division shall, not later than the fifteenth day of each month, submit to the Deputy Commissioner a report setting out the number of applications received, the number approved, the number rejected, and the reasons for rejection. The Deputy Commissioner may require more frequent reports where circumstances warrant.

8.5 Pending the appointment of a full-time Director, the Deputy Commissioner may designate an officer of the Bureau to act as Director of the Heritage Grants Division. Any officer so designated shall have the same powers and duties as a Director appointed under paragraph 8.3(a).

8.6 The Heritage Grants Division shall adopt such forms and procedures as the Deputy Commissioner may approve for the submission of applications and the disbursement of funds. All forms shall be made available to the public at the Bureau’s office and, where practicable, through the Bureau’s liaison officers.

ARTICLE IX — THE RECORDS AND ACCESS DIVISION

9.1 The Records and Access Division shall be responsible for the custody, preservation, and organisation of all records in the possession of the Bureau, including those transferred to the Bureau by government departments, family associations, and private donors.

9.2 The Records and Access Division shall:

(a) maintain the central catalogue of all records held by the Bureau;

(b) supervise the reading room and the reproduction services;

