(c) administer the rules governing access to records, including the classification of records as open, restricted, or closed;

(d) prepare finding aids and guides for the use of researchers;

(e) advise the Deputy Commissioner on the declassification of records.

9.3 The Records and Access Division shall be headed by the Registrar, who shall also perform the functions of Director of that Division. The Registrar shall be assisted by such Archivists and Research Officers as may be appointed under Article V.

ARTICLE X — THE RESEARCH AND PUBLICATIONS DIVISION

10.1 The Research and Publications Division shall be responsible for the conduct of research into family heritage and genealogy, and for the publication of works arising from such research.

10.2 The functions of the Research and Publications Division shall include:

(a) undertaking studies of family histories, clan origins, and migration patterns;

(b) compiling and maintaining biographical and genealogical indexes;

(c) preparing manuscripts for publication, including the Bureau’s quarterly journal and occasional monographs;

(d) organising seminars, workshops, and exhibitions for the dissemination of research findings;

(e) cooperating with universities and learned societies in the advancement of genealogical scholarship.
